{"Title":"An Act exempting disabled veterans from sales tax when leasing a motor vehicle","BillNumber":"H2799","DocketNumber":"HD162","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"WCG1","Name":"William C. Galvin","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WCG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T13:47:28.28"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"WCG1","Name":"William C. Galvin","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WCG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T13:47:28.28"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2799/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Galvin of Canton, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2799) of William C. Galvin for legislation to exempt disabled veterans from the motor vehicle leasing sales tax.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tSection 6 of chapter 64H of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2014 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out subsection (u) and inserting in place thereof the following subsection:-\r\n\t(u) Sale of a motor vehicle purchased by or leased to and for the use of a person who has suffered loss, or permanent loss of use of, both legs or both arms or one leg and one arm or purchased by or leased to and for the use of a veteran who has been determined to be permanently disabled by the medical advisory board established pursuant to section 8C of chapter 90 and has been issued a disabled veteran number plate pursuant to section 2 of said chapter 90. This exemption shall apply to 1 motor vehicle only owned or leased and registered for the personal, noncommercial use of such person.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}